529
00:18:36,240 --> 00:18:38,560
-你看起来是个好小伙 -谢谢
- Now, you seem like a nice guy. - Thanks.

530
00:18:38,860 --> 00:18:40,900
但我并不认为你适合在我家干活儿
But I don't think you're the best fit for this house.

531
00:18:40,900 --> 00:18:44,080
-你 你是认真的吗 -恐怕是的
- Are -- are you serious? - I'm afraid so.

532
00:18:44,080 --> 00:18:44,520
好吧
Okay.

533
00:18:45,460 --> 00:18:46,640
是因为我给你熨了内裤 是吗
It was the underpants, wasn't it?

534
00:18:46,660 --> 00:18:47,440
有这个原因
That didn't help.

535
00:18:47,600 --> 00:18:50,100
我做得太过了 该死
Man, I came on too strong. Gosh dang it!

536
00:18:50,480 --> 00:18:52,500
在我14岁时我爸就警告过我
My dad warned me about that when I turned 14.

537
00:18:52,620 --> 00:18:55,360
他说 "孩子 你将成为一家之主
He said, "Son, you're about to be the man of the family.

538
00:18:55,360 --> 00:18:56,740
你得给别人一些时间
You got to learn to give people time

539
00:18:56,740 --> 00:18:57,800
来看到你的好"
to see how special you are."

540
00:18:57,980 --> 00:18:59,100
为什么你是一家之主
Why were you the man of the family?

541
00:18:59,980 --> 00:19:01,680
-他去世了 -因为什么呢
- He sort of died. - How?

542
00:19:02,020 --> 00:19:03,760
我不想让你不开心 小鬼
I don't want to bring you down, little man.

543
00:19:04,220 --> 00:19:05,040
我爸当初也一样
Neither did my dad.

544
00:19:05,120 --> 00:19:07,280
他说 "我的病和'答案'的发音押韵
He'd say, "My disease can't be all bad

545
00:19:07,280 --> 00:19:08,400
因此也不全是坏事"
if it rhymes with 'answer.'"

546
00:19:10,500 --> 00:19:12,760
我烤的亚麻籽松饼好了
Those are the flaxseed muffins that I just baked.

547
00:19:13,260 --> 00:19:15,960
我把它们拿出来就走
I'll just take them out and get out of here.

548
00:19:15,980 --> 00:19:16,820
安迪 等等
Andy, wait.

549
00:19:18,580 --> 00:19:19,680
我们不会吃的
We're never gonna eat them.

550
00:19:20,620 --> 00:19:23,260
那么 好吧 抱歉我没有做好
Well, then... I'm sorry it didn't work out.

551
00:19:23,260 --> 00:19:24,680
什么没做好
What didn't work out?

552
00:19:24,940 --> 00:19:25,960
我在这里的使命
My mission here.

553
00:19:26,549 --> 00:19:28,595
真的很高兴认识你 普夫人
It was really nice to meet you, though, Mrs. P.

554
00:19:29,300 --> 00:19:31,360
你连一个机会都不给他
You didn't even give him a chance.

555
00:19:31,400 --> 00:19:32,260
我们投过票了的 妈妈
We took a vote, mom.

556
00:19:32,260 --> 00:19:33,580
你得尊重投票
You got to respect the vote.

557
00:19:33,580 --> 00:19:36,200
不 你让我雇那些我不喜欢的保姆
No! You make me hire these nannies that I don't like.

558
00:19:36,200 --> 00:19:38,780
现在我找到一个喜欢的 你又要辞了他
But when I find one that I like, you fire him?!

559
00:19:38,800 --> 00:19:41,720
我才是在这屋子里花时间最多的人
I am the one that spends most of the time around here!

560
00:19:41,720 --> 00:19:43,380
所以该由我来决定
SO I GET TO PICK!

561
00:19:45,120 --> 00:19:48,560
有些时候我们的声音越大 越不被理解
Sometimes the louder we are, the less we're heard.

562
00:19:48,900 --> 00:19:51,080
-你现在很沮丧 对吗 -没错
- You're frustrated right now, aren't you? - Yes.

563
00:19:51,080 --> 00:19:53,840
因为你觉得他们不理解你
Because you feel like they're not hearing you.

564
00:19:54,460 --> 00:19:55,060
没错
Yes.

565
00:19:56,340 --> 00:19:58,160
这也正是他们的感受
Well, that's exactly how they feel.

566
00:20:00,740 --> 00:20:03,080
抱歉我忽略了你们的感受
I'm sorry that I ignored your feelings.

567
00:20:05,060 --> 00:20:07,800
我保证不会再这样咆哮了
I promise that I will try not to yell so much.

568
00:20:08,620 --> 00:20:10,160
-你被录用了 -什么
- You're hired. - What?!

569
00:20:10,280 --> 00:20:12,580
你最好喝了那奶昔 我们要去跑步了
You better drink that smoothie. We're going on a run!

570
00:20:13,260 --> 00:20:14,200
这事儿还没完
This isn't over.

571
00:20:16,000 --> 00:20:17,120
生活并不容易
Life isn't easy.

572
00:20:17,820 --> 00:20:20,040
有时我们只是需要一点点帮助
Sometimes we just need a little help,

573
00:20:20,440 --> 00:20:22,520
来重拾自信
getting your confidence back,

574
00:20:22,820 --> 00:20:24,320
来达成一致
getting on the same page,

575
00:20:25,960 --> 00:20:27,580
来释放自己
getting out of your own way,

576
00:20:33,080 --> 00:20:35,500
或者就是运动起来
or just getting moving.

577
00:20:35,720 --> 00:20:37,560
我很高兴来做这个帮手
And I'm pleased as punch to be the one --

578
00:20:37,600 --> 00:20:39,740
够了 你不念叨都够累了
Okay, this is tough enough without all the yammering!

579
00:20:40,260 --> 00:20:40,780
抱歉
Sorry.

580
00:20:45,680 --> 00:20:47,500
你想要什么伴舞音乐
What would you like to dance to?

581
00:20:47,500 --> 00:20:50,500
我得告诉你 我们要跳方块舞
I have to tell you we have to have some sort of square dancing.

582
00:20:51,020 --> 00:20:51,960
不要放乡村音乐
We're not doing country.

583
00:20:51,960 --> 00:20:53,283
不要方块舞 不要
No square dancing. We're not.

584
00:20:53,283 --> 00:20:55,700
今晚不会有方块舞舞会 胡娇和我
There will be no hoedown tonight. Pepper and I are on...

585
00:20:55,700 --> 00:20:57,660
我的家人会大发脾气
My family is going to throw a fit.

586
00:20:57,660 --> 00:20:59,180
-他们会捣乱 -我们不是为他们而婚
- They'll riot. - We're not getting married for them.

587
00:20:59,180 --> 00:21:00,420
我们是为自己结婚
We're getting married for us.

588
00:21:00,540 --> 00:21:02,320
我觉得我们应该有一个多层裱花蛋糕
And I think we have a decorative cake out front,

589
00:21:02,320 --> 00:21:03,820
再在后面放一个单层蛋糕
and then we have sheet cakes in the back.

590
00:21:03,940 --> 00:21:06,460
我知道你想要什么主题了
Oh, I see! Is that the theme you're going for

591
00:21:06,720 --> 00:21:07,140
土气主题
-- tacky?!

592
00:21:07,240 --> 00:21:07,920
"单层的" 像床单那样铺开的
Sheet -- like a sheet.

593
00:21:08,040 --> 00:21:08,700
"单层的"啊
Oh, "Sheet."

594
00:21:08,700 --> 00:21:10,520
我还以为你说的是"花哨的"
I thought he said "Chic cake."

595
00:21:10,700 --> 00:21:13,560
我的蛋糕都很花哨
All of my cakes are chic.
